bombastic.<br /> Ther is no need to capitalize words, or make a scene with imaginary whisky glass for make your points.<br /> <br /> This give the impression of mere rants and piss off readers from your very valid content.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I personally thought the dramatic tone makes thing lighter and more fun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T09:39:49-07:00","id":1344005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344002#post1344002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally thought the dramatic tone makes thing lighter and more fun</div> </div> </div> </div>Another very valid point too! This must be very subjective, of course.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T10:26:33-07:00","id":1344013,"title":"","content":"What can I say, I've got a style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T10:53:54-07:00","id":1344021,"title":"","content":"This is certainly an excellent exposition of how ghosts are monstrous, and how ghost-like the Bound are, and I'm not about to reject it.<br /> <br /> A small counterpoint, though. Geist 2e <i>contains</i> all this material, but it doesn't exactly <i>emphasize</i> it. Ghosts in the text are typically shown, and coded, as victims (of an all-consuming Underworld, and of necromancers both mundane and Bound), not as dangerous in themselves. Hence the &quot;social justice necromancers&quot; crack. And the Bound are distinctly alien, driven by Burdens and geists, but they're not inherently predatory - not even as much as 2e changelings are. (Never mind what vampires and Beasts - the true predators on humanity - do to people.)<br /> <br /> Measured by the axis of internal vs. external monstrosity, Geist 2e is a long way out on the external end, past where Werewolf, Changeling and Demon are. Vampire and Beast, by contrast, are at the internal end (Beast more than Vampire) and even Mage ends up on the internal side more often than not. (Deviant could swing either way IMO. The default Renegade game is biased to external horror, a Devoted game would probably swing to internal.) So the people talking about Sin-eaters as little rays of sunshine in a grim confusing world do have a point - it's based on tone and emphasis, not all the established facts, but that tone and emphasis are really there in the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T11:18:24-07:00","id":1344026,"title":"","content":"*lured by having Yuki Kaijura at the music choice*<br /> <br /> I just want to ask- was there really a discussion where people claimed that Sin Eaters are <i>not </i>monsters? I mean, I was aware about it in some of the other gamelines you have mentioned- but really? <i>Sin Eaters</i>? Like- how?..<br /> <br /> Never mind that. I should not have been surprised by it, and yet here we are. Anyway, yeah, of course they are monsters- and that is the beauty of them. One of my favorite changes from 1e to 2e was the concept of the Bound as being soulless- it brought an whole new twist about the Bound condition, sending them with one foot in the grave while laughing behind their masks. It emphasized that yes, Sin Eaters are dead, and yes, you are ghost, and yes, of course you are a monster if you ever thought otherwise. It brought an whole new level of nihilism to the heart of the Bound, just as well as the rest of the book did an excellent job at darkening the world of Geist, from the ever hungry Underworld and to the everyday tragedy of the dead around you. That darkness, actually, made their light shine even brighter than before- you had a second chance, which may very well be your last one at achieving what that kept you dead and kicking. Make sure you used it correctly.<br /> <br /> That reminds me that one time, when I walked in the middle of a storm. The rain was hitting me from all sides at the same time, and my umbrella was nothing more than a decoration in that strong wind. I tried to find escape from time to time, but the rain wasn't going to end anytime soon, and the water level in the streets got up to my knees. I remember trying to fight against the storm, trying to keep at least some part of me dry- but eventually, I was soaked to my bones- and with that, I suddenly realized that there was nothing worse that the storm could have done to me. I reached the bottom- and by that, I was free to just walk down the street on my way home, laughing at the people who still watched the rain in terror. Suddenly, I became free.<br /> <br /> And if that's what surviving a mere storm can do to you- what about literally losing everything? What about having to practically die- only to return? What kind of freedom would that grant you? What kind of norm or law could actually stand in your way to achieve what you truly desire?<br /> <br /> I can't believe that some people think that Sin Eaters are not monsters. How could they <i>not</i> be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 10-27-2019, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T11:25:59-07:00","id":1344027,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1133\" data-vbnamecard=\"1133\">Michael Brazier</a> : Oh yeah, that's absolutely true. Now, mind you, I wholly endorse that take for the core book. I think it create a god distinction from the other gamelines and helps to really direct Geist where before it was perhaps more listless. Now that said, I also think the supplements from here on are going to need to be willing to dive back into that internal horror and tragedy, remind the audience that if you want good guys, you gotta put in the work. No one gets a free ride.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1343996#post1343996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*applause*<br /> <br /> This needs to be posted everywhere. Or at least a soundbite which really encapsulates why I dislike a lot of humanocentric horror;<br /> <br /> &quot;MONSTER DOES NOT MEAN BAD PERSON. IT MEANS 'EASILY TEMPTED TO DO BAD THINGS' PERSON. THAT DOES NOT MAKE THEN NOT PEOPLE. THANK YOU.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well now, let's keep in mind that the Chronicles is philosophically driven by humanism-the above points still do not deny the horror of these entities to human people or the horror of being those people, all of which comes back around to relaying the importance of humanity over supernatural sources.<br /> <br /> If you would <i>actually</i> rather be one of the monsters than human, then the point is missed-which is why Mage is a Very Frustrating Conversation Piece.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344026#post1344026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just want to ask- was there really a discussion where people claimed that Sin Eaters are <i>not </i>monsters? I mean, I was aware about it in some of the other gamelines you have mentioned- but really? <i>Sin Eaters</i>? Like- how?..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it happened. It's actually happened in snippets here and there all over the place. That quote I use to start off the conversation on ghosts(not the Alan Moore one, the other one) is a real quote-there's more to it, but I reached the end of the selected and my brain bluescreened for a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-27-2019, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T11:29:09-07:00","id":1344029,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Double Post, blegh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T11:41:00-07:00","id":1344032,"title":"","content":"Unauthorized Summary: &quot;The splats in CoD are not <i>character classes.</i> They are storylines.&quot; <br /> <br /> This is why I am leery of mixing different CoD game lines. I imagine that it can be done, but IMO each splat has its own narrative drives and it would be hard to reconcile several of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T12:08:39-07:00","id":1344037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344027#post1344027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well now, let's keep in mind that the Chronicles is philosophically driven by humanism-the above points still do not deny the horror of these entities to human people or the horror of being those people, all of which comes back around to relaying the importance of humanity over supernatural sources.<br /> <br /> If you would <i>actually</i> rather be one of the monsters than human, then the point is missed-which is why Mage is a Very Frustrating Conversation Piece.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I would rather have supernatural powers <i>in the context of the CofD. </i>The ideal would be to live happily in ignorance, but if I'm caught in the storm I'd rather be flying in the wind rather than tossed around by it. It's simply a practical choice for agency rather than a desire to sip blood for eternity, be prone to Death Rage, or have to constantly calculate risk of Paradox if I want to access my powers.<br /> <br /> By &quot;humanocentrism&quot; I mean &quot;Humanity Fuck Yeah,&quot; which can easily become &quot;Everyone Else Can Get Fucked&quot;, which isn't just boring to read, it's also kinda vaguely creepy if you start seeing analogies to actual humans in the Everyone Else. Also because a lot of Gothic Horror is founded on Victorian Horror, which includes stuff like &quot;madness means you're <s>unpresentable</s> evil and creepy!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T12:09:40-07:00","id":1344038,"title":"","content":"@ Keiran: Ish?<br /> <br /> Unrelated, this thread also needs some Rob Zombie, so have some <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BvsMPOfblfg\" target=\"_blank\">Living Dead Girl</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-27-2019, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T17:09:33-07:00","id":1344096,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11876\" data-vbnamecard=\"11876\">Deinos</a>, you asked, here ya go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T18:40:19-07:00","id":1344108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew#post1343937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*sigh*<br /> ...<br /> Still, someone's got to kick the pipes back in place, even if they whimper piteously as you do so. Sin-eater's gotta sin. I guess that makes it time for Arcane to explain the obvious again, as is my talent and cross to bear. Let's talk about how Sin-Eaters are Monsters, and quite often still kind of bad people at the least.<br /> ...<br /> I actually think this conversation is really dumb.<br /> <br /> I feel like I need to explain this, but I <i>really</i> think I'm wasting my time by explaining something <i>ridiculously and stupidly simple</i>. I'm kind of flabbergasted I feel like I need to lay this out. This is the hardest &quot;Of Course X is a Monster&quot; post I've ever had to get into, because <i>Jesus Christ bouncing up and down on the Purple Man's meat pole</i> what world would I ever need to explain ghosts as monsters in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, it must suck to constantly start arguments because you feel the need to remind everyone how they're having fun wrong and bring it up constantly, but to hate doing it. Like, if you were hostile all the time because it gave you enjoyment to cut people down, that's understandable, but apparently you hate it.<br /> <br /> I kind of feel as if responding to a lengthly piece about how someone considers me to be stupid and wasting his time is just going to lead to more dismissive emotes and insults, but one thing I will point out because it needs to be said: Burdens are a Sin Eater thing. They're not a rank 2 ghost thing. Rank 2 ghosts can very easily wind up with no connection to their former existence whatsoever, let alone wanting to resolve unfinished business from it. The ephemera known as ghosts and sin eaters recognizably have to do with tropes about ghost stories, but the ephemera known as ghosts don't have the majority fixation on moving on you are attributing to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T19:14:02-07:00","id":1344112,"title":"","content":"A ghost with no connection to its former existence, as you put it, is invariably pulled into the Underworld through the nearest Avernian Gate. Any ghost that's capable of staying in the living world at all <i>must</i> have some overriding purpose to keep them anchored there, so they conform to ArcaneArts' description.<br /> <br /> Sure, if you go into the Underworld you can find ghosts that aren't obsessed with unfinished business from their living days - but if you're not a supernatural being, how are you getting into the Underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T20:11:09-07:00","id":1344115,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344038#post1344038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Keiran: Ish?<br /> <br /> Unrelated, this thread also needs some Rob Zombie, so have some <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BvsMPOfblfg\" target=\"_blank\">Living Dead Girl</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um.... Assuming that you are referencing me... I'm not sure how to parse &quot;Ish?&quot;<ul><li>&quot;Ish&quot; = sorta?</li> <li>&quot;Ish&quot; = Issue? (as in, &quot;what's your issue, pal?&quot;)</li> <li>&quot;Ish&quot; = Issue&quot; (as in, &quot;what issue are you citing?&quot;)</li> </ul>Anyway, your long and interesting essay reminded me (tangentially) of a problem in AI: any utility function (as in &quot;please maximize this thing here&quot;) for a suitably powerful AI leads to disaster. An AI asked to maximize the number of staples produced at a staple factory might eventually harvest the metallic core of the Earth to make staples. A human wouldn't do that because they have other priorities (such as not killing all life on Earth, etc.) Your description of ghosts points out that they may lack compensating priorities when dealing with their own unresolved issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-27T22:39:38-07:00","id":1344131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344112#post1344112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A ghost with no connection to its former existence, as you put it, is invariably pulled into the Underworld through the nearest Avernian Gate. Any ghost that's capable of staying in the living world at all <i>must</i> have some overriding purpose to keep them anchored there, so they conform to ArcaneArts' description.<br /> <br /> Sure, if you go into the Underworld you can find ghosts that aren't obsessed with unfinished business from their living days - but if you're not a supernatural being, how are you getting into the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>And as a result of this your ghost turns into a absent which to be honest kind of makes them less human seeing as they trade memories with other ghost including there very own to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T14:42:28-07:00","id":1344261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344115#post1344115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um.... Assuming that you are referencing me... I'm not sure how to parse &quot;Ish?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the first one.<br /> <br /> &quot;Unchained demon&quot; may not be a character class, but it's also not a story<i>line</i> on its own \u2014 an Integrator and a Saboteur deal with similar problems by virtue of being the same type of entity, but their arcs run the gamut from weirdly similar to utterly antithetical. A Devoted serving as a quality-control regulator for the rare well-meaning conspiracy in the Web of Pain deals with the same pitfalls of human cruelty and obsession that a more conventional Renegade does, but they also may never trip the switch into the latter mode of play even as the former gets recruited into the position of Mob legbreaker through their Loyalty Touchstones. A Daeva and a Gangrel approach undeath in dramatically different ways just by virtue of their curses and powerset.<br /> <br /> For the same reason, you <i>can</i> link up characters in different gamelines through different focal themes and moods \u2014 body horror alone is present as an angle in half the lines, and alienation likewise, to say nothing of more particular questions like &quot;how much do you privilege your own needs and fears over your neighbor's?&quot; or &quot;what are you willing to do to achieve your goals?&quot; or &quot;do you trust other monsters to have a say in your affairs?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T14:57:16-07:00","id":1344263,"title":"","content":"^ That, that's the intention.<br /> <br /> EDIT: BTW, anyone wanna tell me where I exactly said people were having badwrongfun or how explaining how Sin-Eaters still fulfill the thematic and tonal core of the Chronicles overall constitutes violating Geist's themes or telling people they're having badwrong fun?<br /> <br /> Cause I cannot, for the life of me, find a single instance I said that or otherwise did that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-28-2019, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T22:05:18-07:00","id":1344348,"title":"","content":"This is great, and I need to avoid to that screaming voice inside me that says &quot;yeah, but that's not how being a person works&quot; because the way I relate to being a human/person/Me is odd and is pretty N/A to 90 percent of people. Still a dash more negative then I'd take the spalt, but this is nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-28T23:13:45-07:00","id":1344355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalzky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344348#post1344348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is great, and I need to avoid to that screaming voice inside me that says &quot;yeah, but that's not how being a person works&quot; because the way I relate to being a human/person/Me is odd and is pretty N/A to 90 percent of people. Still a dash more negative then I'd take the spalt, but this is nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's way more negative than I read the splat, usually.<br /> <br /> My point isn't that this the all-consuming end-all, be-all point to Sin-Eaters, that altruism is a joke and that everything you think is shit.<br /> <br /> My point is that the inherent monstrosity of the splat and it's focuses enhance it's own themes and reinforce the humanism at the core of Chronicles. The entire franchise is actually rather optimistic and empathetic on the whole, but it does so by diving through hell and emerging on the other side rather than flirting with the shore of the Ocean of Fragments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-29-2019, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T06:10:05-07:00","id":1344396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344112#post1344112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A ghost with no connection to its former existence, as you put it, is invariably pulled into the Underworld through the nearest Avernian Gate. Any ghost that's capable of staying in the living world at all <i>must</i> have some overriding purpose to keep them anchored there, so they conform to ArcaneArts' description.<br /> <br /> Sure, if you go into the Underworld you can find ghosts that aren't obsessed with unfinished business from their living days - but if you're not a supernatural being, how are you getting into the Underworld?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how ghosts work. They have anchors and memories, but these may or may not be of relevance to their old life; mages, sin eaters, and anyone with a ceremony can work as an anchor. They aren't stated or implied to be obsessed with unfinished business, that's sin eaters (both halves of them). Don't mix up SEs and ghosts psychologically; SEs have a burden and are inexorably tied to their pasts and human identity, but ghosts aren't mentally at all like disembodied sin eaters.<br /> <br /> If you have the time, you may as well grant a ghost plenty of extra anchors. They aren't becoming obsessive freaks about them, they're simply a source of strength. People becoming ghosts are the norm in CofD, not the product of a frantic and diseased mind.<br /> <br /> A sin eater's burden is why they accepted the bargain (afaik). They were probably going to become a ghost even without that intensity, because nearly everyone becomes a ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T08:09:03-07:00","id":1344417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew#post1343937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a more idle and speculative side of things, <i>I</i> definitely take the side of basically more things being Monsters than Not-really, I leave it at Mortal Investigators without Supernatural Merits as being the only things that aren't Monsters unless their actions and mindsets push them over into being Monsters of that sort. I admit that's some ice to stand on, but on the other hand, I'm a Beast fan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I enjoyed your essay, and was wondering if you might post your take on the Vampire game. I ask because, while they are obviously monsters, I usually only see them interpreted as cool, sexy, power-tripping supernaturals. I don't play VtR, so this is merely an outside view. However, it's also one of the reasons why the game holds little interest for me. But perhaps I have a wrong impression, and I'd be interested in your view of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T11:44:55-07:00","id":1344458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344396#post1344396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how ghosts work. They have anchors and memories, but these may or may not be of relevance to their old life; mages, sin eaters, and anyone with a ceremony can work as an anchor. They aren't stated or implied to be obsessed with unfinished business, that's sin eaters (both halves of them). Don't mix up SEs and ghosts psychologically; SEs have a burden and are inexorably tied to their pasts and human identity, but ghosts aren't mentally at all like disembodied sin eaters.<br /> <br /> If you have the time, you may as well grant a ghost plenty of extra anchors. They aren't becoming obsessive freaks about them, they're simply a source of strength. People becoming ghosts are the norm in CofD, not the product of a frantic and diseased mind.<br /> <br /> A sin eater's burden is why they accepted the bargain (afaik). They were probably going to become a ghost even without that intensity, because nearly everyone becomes a ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem: Sin-Eaters are ghosts. You are literally a ghost who got a once in a (second)lifetime opportunity. You are a ghost is possessing your own body with a co-pilot who's covered in thick layers of dust. Sin-Eaters are ghosts of people who decided that making a deal with monstrous little god of death who can only socialize through fear and intimidation and you have little evidence of being human ever was, in fact, a deal worth making-Which, hey, I get, but it also says something about the sort of people who make that deal. Not every ghost accepts the Bargain, and for good reasons.<br /> <br /> Anyways, point is you're a ghost. And with being a ghost comes being a Being Who Knows They've Got Shit to Do About That Being.<br /> <br /> Rank 2 Ghosts may have the most retained humanity and therefore the most ability to fallafle about and be distracted from it, but every ghost exists to handle the last affairs of the dead, and they all <i>know </i>that they've got that shit to deal with, and the consequences of not doing it-everyone's aware of what it means to lose their anchors without resolving them, in involves the sinkhole gate in the graveyard down the block and the black maw that slowly chews up the dead that pass into it. Rank 1 ghosts are condemned to the repetition of the one act most likely to resolve that affair, while Rank 3 Geists literally forget everything but the edges of their hangup, but the Memories that Burn Bright Enough to cast a shadow of a ghost onto the world that every ghost knows they've got the shit to deal with.<br /> <br /> Now they(rank 2 and above ghosts) can <i>run</i> from that, or <i>ignore</i> them-the sort of emotional and social situations that wrap themselves up into anchors tend to be complicated and, well, burdensome, the sort of thing that you might not want to confront, and that's normal-but it's not like ghosts don't know there's something they regret that needs to be resolved.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the world of the dead and dying isn't, shall we say, brimming with opportunities to neglect the important things in your life-again, that sinkhole opens and sucks down things that lose their ability to retain themselves in the Twilight, and being away from your anchor is the equivalent of walking out into a Below Zero Snowstorm. You kind of have to hang around the things that were important enough that you essential self decided to forge them into the wellspring of existence your arbiter would rely on. As you lose more and more things, you often have no choice but to fixate more and more on your problem-old ghosts tend to lose sight of anything outside of the matters of their anchors for a reason, and that's because they realize more and more as it goes on that their anchors are basically the only thing of the world that matters.<br /> <br /> You also tend to escalate the more those things aren't resolved, because desperation starts creeping in as the you lose anchors and you keep missing Reapers and the Other Things That Stalk You In the Dark and people start forgetting you and the world begins to slowly fall apart. It's becomes easy to see it as not being enough to leave messages in the walls-maybe you gotta scratch your pleas into flesh in order for someone to do something. It's not enough to talk through lights, maybe they'll find the deposit if you throw lamps around and chase them to it. If something fails, you gotta do more, because a second death is coming, and the world on the otherside of the sinkhole is the worst of the main other worlds out there.<br /> <br /> And all of that is before you account for the way that even rank 2 ghosts can have their memories eaten, stolen, traded, and lost in general-but the anchors remain, and more importantly the reason behind them remains. A Ghost may not Remember Why This Matters, but they know there is something that remains that Matters, and that it's the reason they're there, and most will reach the conclusion they should Do Something About That before Things Get Worse.<br /> <br /> A ghost's natural anchors are, in the end, just a physical representation of that Thing That Matters What Binds Them To This Second Life. In this way, even when they persist on artificially constructed anchors, even if they loose their inherent anchors, they've still got the shit to deal with, that thing of regret they must resolve. All new or changed anchors do is make it harder for them*.<br /> <br /> Burdens are a neat way of codifying those urges and issues that cause a ghost to form in the first place that plays nicely with the X-splat conceit and codifying them along with powersets that evoke the conflict that players can latch onto and use, but every ghost has it(maybe not so neatly summarized, but Storyteller's can use burdens to describe why a ghost remains just as easily), and the reason Sin-eaters have them is because every ghost has them. It's useful design-and-play shorthand.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: Uh, yeah, every ghost has a burden, and they live in circumstances that drive them to pursue it, and as the condition of being dead continues to warp them the long they go at it, the more those ghosts are going to obsess over them and escalate in trying to get them to resolve, because the alternative is the Underworld, and boy howdy, does no one want that. Sin-Eaters are ghosts who decided that making a deal with a Intimidating and Frightful Small Death God for a second shot at life is Not A Bad Deal, and that does say some things about them. Nothing damning, but nothing comfortable either.<br /> <br /> But every ghost, Sin-Eater or not, knows they've got shit to deal with, and they know the world is against them in terms of getting that shit done. Sin-Eaters just have it metaphysically codified so it's easier for players.<br /> <br /> *Usually, sometimes an anchor is provided to make things easier, but necromancers outside of Sin-Eaters being hyper-concerned for ghosts is a coin toss.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KieranMullen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344417#post1344417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoyed your essay, and was wondering if you might post your take on the Vampire game. I ask because, while they are obviously monsters, I usually only see them interpreted as cool, sexy, power-tripping supernaturals. I don't play VtR, so this is merely an outside view. However, it's also one of the reasons why the game holds little interest for me. But perhaps I have a wrong impression, and I'd be interested in your view of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>My take is that Vampire the Requiem Second Edition/Blood and Smoke does a marvelous job of explaining and exploring how they're monsters and what that means for them and how we might enhance the fun or learn more about ourselves in the Kindred, and reading that will solve most problems.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't exactly see developing trends of people simply understanding a misconception and not acknowledging the realities of vampires being monsters and not being good people, and that makes it hard to get personally riled up enough to get into Explanation Mode.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-29-2019, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-29T11:48:40-07:00","id":1344459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344396#post1344396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not how ghosts work. They have anchors and memories, but these may or may not be of relevance to their old life; mages, sin eaters, and anyone with a ceremony can work as an anchor. They aren't stated or implied to be obsessed with unfinished business, that's sin eaters (both halves of them).</div> </div> </div> </div>Deinos. Open up your advance PDF and search for the phrase &quot;unfinished business.&quot;<br /> <br /> It shows up a lot! Including <i>in the Anchor Condition writeup that is largely unchanged from its first appearance in the GMC Rules Appendix six years ago.</i><br /> <br /> You are flatly wrong about this point. Objectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T01:43:55-07:00","id":1344609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344458#post1344458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem: Sin-Eaters are ghosts. You are literally a ghost who got a once in a (second)lifetime opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're figuratively ghosts (much in the same way that ghosts are figuratively souls or spirits), and based off ghost story tropes like a ghost (lets assume I'm talking about rank 2s when I talk about ghosts, as they're the only kind that seem to be playable), but they aren't literally ghosts in a cofd sense and their psychology and parameters winds up being very different. They were presumably about to become ghosts, but didn't.<br /> <br /> The presumption that ghosts who aren't focused on resolution are running from something isn't really in theme with GtSE2e, only about half are portrayed as fixated on their former existence. The rest are about a new existence that is just as legitimate as corporeal human life. Moving on is good for some people, but not everyone has anything to move on from, which is good since its anyone's guess if there's anything to move on to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344459#post1344459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are flatly wrong about this point. Objectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, &quot;objectively,&quot; meaning &quot;figuratively, but with emphasis.&quot; But since you asked, first two things I noticed about ghosts being stated:<br /> <br /> &quot;she lingered after death not because life left her with unfinished business, but because death itself was her business&quot;<br /> &quot;Ending the condition: Some ghosts cling to Anchors which represent unfinished business.&quot;<br /> <br /> There you go, just because you asked: two examples straight from the book that demonstrate that its a characterization of some ghosts, and not nearly all. Anchors are just defined as &quot;things that bear great significance to the ghost&quot; and &quot;based on whatever subject anchors the ghost's identity.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;This Condition is immediately created when a new ghost is formed, based on whatever subject anchors the ghost\u2019s identity...<br /> Ending the Condition: The easiest way to end an Anchor condition is to destroy the subject. Some ghosts cling to Anchors that represent unfinished business, in which case resolving those issues can remove the Condition&quot;<br /> <br /> tl;dr only some anchors are unfinished business and only some ghosts cling to unfinished business, this is directly stated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T17:52:58-07:00","id":1344785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344609#post1344609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;she lingered after death not because life left her with unfinished business, but because death itself was her business&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>From the example ghost The Professor, whose writeup directly precedes that phrase with &quot;As an anthropologist already fixated on the traditions of death all over the world,&quot; which <i>surely</i> has nothing to do with ghosts being obsessive personlike monsters, especially not for a character whose curiosity is very strongly implied to be pushing her towards geisthood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There you go, just because you asked: two examples straight from the book that demonstrate that its a characterization of some ghosts, and not nearly all. Anchors are just defined as &quot;things that bear great significance to the ghost&quot; and &quot;based on whatever subject anchors the ghost's identity.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Hey, Deinos, quick question: <i>what do you suppose &quot;anchors the ghost's identity&quot; means?</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;This Condition is immediately created when a new ghost is formed, based on whatever subject anchors the ghost\u2019s identity...<br /> Ending the Condition: The easiest way to end an Anchor condition is to destroy the subject. Some ghosts cling to Anchors that represent unfinished business, in which case resolving those issues can remove the Condition&quot; </div> </div> </div>&quot;Anyone with doubts, hidden sins, or unfinished business might find themselves bound to the bones of the earth, tethered to Anchors.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Anchors are people, places, and things that held great significance to the ghost's life or death. Most ghosts have at least one (their own body or grave), and few have more than three.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;An Anchor that is destroyed or dies loses the Anchor Condition. [\u2026] A ghost who loses all her Anchors is immediately and irresistibly blown through the nearest Avernian Gate and into the Underworld.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Resolving an Anchor means that the ghost is willing to let go of that Anchor and move on. Ghosts always know when one of their Anchors is resolved. Resolved Anchors lose the Anchor Condition. [\u2026] A ghost who resolves all her Anchors is no longer subject to Essence bleed and is not dragged into the Underworld. She may Pass On with the appropriate Ceremony.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T19:08:03-07:00","id":1344801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344609#post1344609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're figuratively ghosts (much in the same way that ghosts are figuratively souls or spirits)-</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Stopping you here.<br /> <br /> 1) It's text in the book. It's not even hidden text, it's literally open in the fluff and mechanics of the splat. Read Chapter 2, if nothing else-but also read the bits relating to the metaphysics of Sin-Eaters, like Why Their Memories and Attempts at Honoring the Dead Don't Count For Providing Essence.<br /> 2) It's text in any bit of development talk outside of the book. Feel free to check threads on the subject, particularly preview threads.<br /> 3) I double checked when I was writing the Regalia and Ceremonies chapter for Memento Mori, because while I didn't get to go crazy with assertions in that chapter, I wanted to at least seed ideas for future writers, and while I was I was <i>absolutely sure</i> I was right, I wanted to confirm I was right so I could get away with some of the things I did. And, as it turned out, I did indeed get away with them.<br /> <br /> I can help you deal with interpretations of the text. I can learn and change my point of view based on your interpretations of the text. What I <i>cannot do</i> is change the text, and <i>three times over</i> the text is you are a <i>god damned ghost</i>, and I <i>cannot help you </i>if for some reason you don't want to read the text as it's written.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Like, understand that I can be wrong, but I can't afford to be wrong <i>when it's my job</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-30-2019, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T20:55:31-07:00","id":1345159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344785#post1344785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey, Deinos, quick question: <i>what do you suppose &quot;anchors the ghost's identity&quot; means?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>All sorts of stuff, which doesn't include any assumption that its something the ghost wants or needs to rid itself of.<br /> We've been over this. The condition clearly states that *some* ghosts are tethered to anchors that represent unfinished business. I have no idea how you could read that condition as *all* sharing your preferred characterization.<br /> You also cited a bunch of stuff about anchors that are important to a ghost without portraying them as things the ghost needs or wants to divest itself of. In general, your attempts to corrall all ghosts into one small characterization package would be a missed opportunity as far as portraying ghosts as mattering as people goes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1344801#post1344801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can help you deal with interpretations of the text. I can learn and change my point of view based on your interpretations of the text. What I <i>cannot do</i> is change the text, and <i>three times over</i> the text is you are a <i>god damned ghost</i>, and I <i>cannot help you </i>if for some reason you don't want to read the text as it's written.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Like, understand that I can be wrong, but I can't afford to be wrong <i>when it's my job</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you could change the text, I'm sure you'd put it somewhere that sin eaters are ghosts, since three times over you've<br /> <br /> &quot;Read a development post&quot; is not very &quot;literally open in the fluff and mechanics.&quot; I'm aware that sin eaters are inspired by tropes and such pertaining to ghosts, and are ghosts in the vague, metaphorical, not true in a fluff or mechanics way that ghosts are souls and spirits.<br /> <br /> You can choose to read &quot;metaphysically dead&quot; as &quot;a ghost.&quot; That is one hell of a stretch to me. I would expect a lot of things to be metaphysically dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T21:31:40-07:00","id":1345165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1345159#post1345159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've been over this. The condition clearly states that *some* ghosts are tethered to anchors that represent unfinished business. I have no idea how you could read that condition as *all* sharing your preferred characterization.</div> </div> </div> </div>My &quot;preferred characterization&quot; is that ghosts care about the stuff that made certain things their Anchors and &quot;you can get rid of the Anchor Condition by destroying its subject&quot; doesn't make the crux of Sin-Eating a minority focus of stories dealing with earthbound specters.<br /> <br /> It's completely absurd to claim that the use of particular rather than general language in describing how ghosts are attached to unfinished business means that ghosts, particularly ghosts as they are encountered in Geist, don't have anything to do with the people they exist in direct reference to the vast majority of the time.<br /> <br /> I can tell you a piece of fiction where the metaphysics of ghosts in general have nothing to do with the life they exist after, but the Chronicles of Darkness are not such a piece of fiction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You also cited a bunch of stuff about anchors that are important to a ghost without portraying them as things the ghost needs or wants to divest itself of. In general, your attempts to corrall all ghosts into one small characterization package would be a missed opportunity as far as portraying ghosts as mattering as people goes. </div> </div> </div>The things I cited run as follows:<br /> <br /> 1. Anchors are things that mattered to the life and death of the person from whom a ghost's identity is derived.<br /> 2. These things can lose the qualities that tie a ghost to them either voluntarily or through entropy.<br /> 3. Losing Anchors through entropy eventually dumps a ghost into a place that tries to eat them on a daily basis, which offers very limited means of escape besides drinking acid and horribly scarring themselves (which generally requires a pretty strong motivation and, as Arc points out, brings them <i>more</i> in line with approaching the remnants of their old lives as unfinished business, because every geist has a Remembrance).<br /> 4. Losing Anchors by letting them go voluntarily gives a ghost as much freedom of movement as a geist gets without the need for horrific mutilation and also opens up the chance for the restless dead to finally rest.<br /> <br /> There is nothing for the dead beyond the things that they are fixated upon, the engagement of those with the sight to see them, and the pull of the Underworld. They can't interact with most people without traumatizing them, they can't stray more than a few yards from their Anchors without suffering or letting go of them entirely, the next layer down is a waterlogged scarcity-stricken hell-pit, and the nearest things to safe havens in the Great Below charge an entry fee and only hold the end at bay as long as you adhere to their code of conduct (and only then until they inevitably fall into the Ocean and break apart).<br /> <br /> The kind of person who wants to stick around the Underworld is the kind of person who didn't need the trauma of death to give them a fixation to cling to, or the kind of person who takes suspicious masks presented to them in a place like the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Answer the question properly: What do you think &quot;anchors the ghost's identity&quot; actually means?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-01-2019, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T04:17:15-07:00","id":1345191,"title":"","content":"Ammmmm....<br /> <br /> 1) On the subject of &quot;ghosts growing beyond their obsessive state&quot;- it is really not the theme of the book and the natural course of ghosts in CofD. In general, ghosts have two possible fates- moving on, or being eaten by the Underworld. Well, that, and getting drown in the Ocean of Fragments. Sure, they can find ways to get around it- they can sacrifice a measure of their self and become Geists. They can sacrifice their freedom and become Reapers. They can sacrifice their memories and become Absent. And they can hover constantly around their Anchors and demand to be remembered. Three of those options make them less and less human- not actually evolving, as much as forgetting who they are, just in order to survive. The last is, as Arc describes, becoming obsessive individuals who will do anything to escape the Great Bellow. Trading in memories is not a way for ghosts to &quot;grow and evolve&quot;. It is a way to sacrifice who you are and everything you have just to get some extra time before the inevitable will happen and you will be eaten by the Underworld. Even the Dead Dominions, where ghosts can find solace as long as they follow the Old Laws, would eventually collapse into the Ocean. The Underworld is the last place a ghost would want to go to, and which would do anything they can in order to escape.<br /> <br /> 2) When a ghost is formed, its Anchors are naturally things which the ghost found as important in life. Or else, why would they get attached to those places in the first place? You say &quot;ghosts can have anchors which are not related to their life&quot;, something which is literally not support by either the text or by ghost stories in both folklore and fiction in general. After losing Anchors, IIRC, ghosts don't just produce new ones to replace them- which means they have less why to gain Essence, and are more likely to lose their hold over the living world. they have to find a way out as soon as possible- and in the meanwhile, they must make sure that their Anchors are safe, and that they have enough Essence to survive and protect them. Anchors which are produced by magic, be it Awakened, Ceremonial or anything else, is not considered to be a &quot;natural way to get Anchors&quot;. Ghost being obsessed over their Anchors is not just a CofD thing, it is a ghost stories thing, and trying to claim otherwise makes little sense since Geist is a game for ghost stories.<br /> <br /> 3) Sin Eaters are soulless beings. Ghosts are soulless beings. While the Geist is riding the body, it is not the one to control- you till operate there, without a soul. Something made the Bargain with the Geist, and that something was heavily hinted, if not outright stated, to be the ghost. I mean, everything about Sin Eaters fits the description of a ghost- from their burdens to their detachment from the world of the living, the fact that they can channel the powers of death and, of course, the fact that they died. Something which dead and has no soul, bound to solve their burdens from their previous lives? yeah, I think that is the definition for a ghost in CofD.<br /> <br /> Like, you'll need some very, very creative reading of the text to ignore the obvious intention of the writers and developers about those subjects, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T04:42:30-07:00","id":1345197,"title":"","content":"In the usually copy-pasted ephemeral entity rules it's quite clear that ghosts are supposed to obsess over their Anchors as unfinished business, but most of that was left out when the section was rewritten for Geist 2e. In fact, iirc, it's even said in GtSE that some Rank 1 ghosts completely unaware of their Anchor while they go along with their usual routine. I.e. the Anchor only anchors the ghost's existence to this world, but it has no emotional value for them.<br /> <br /> As for Bound as ghosts, it's afaik never once outright stated. Ghost stories about obsession after death is 100% a huge part or the themes of the game and the splat, but if they're not confirmed to be ghosts then they simply do not inform the nature of actual ghosts in the setting.<br /> And yes, I'm fully aware of the dev comment, but if it never made it into the book (as more than a mere suggestion) then it's merely one possible interpretation. Death of the author, and all that.<br /> But if it <i>is</i> stated in the book and I've just missed it, then feel free to correct me.<br /> <br /> As for being metaphysically dead; so are a lot of things in CofD without being ghosts. Vampires being the most obvious example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T17:33:48-07:00","id":1345356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1345191#post1345191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, ghosts have two possible fates- moving on, or being eaten by the Underworld. Well, that, and getting drown in the Ocean of Fragments. Sure, they can find ways to get around it- they can sacrifice a measure of their self and become Geists. They can sacrifice their freedom and become Reapers. They can sacrifice their memories and become Absent. And they can hover constantly around their Anchors and demand to be remembered. Three of those options make them less and less human- not actually evolving, as much as forgetting who they are, just in order to survive. The last is, as Arc describes, becoming obsessive individuals who will do anything to escape the Great Bellow. Trading in memories is not a way for ghosts to &quot;grow and evolve&quot;. It is a way to sacrifice who you are and everything you have just to get some extra time before the inevitable will happen and you will be eaten by the Underworld. Even the Dead Dominions, where ghosts can find solace as long as they follow the Old Laws, would eventually collapse into the Ocean. The Underworld is the last place a ghost would want to go to, and which would do anything they can in order to escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding to this, there's one more thing that ghosts can do that's arguably even more insidious than becoming a Reaper:<br /> <br /> The Ferrymen are a self-perpetuating manifestation of the Underworld's hunger.<br /> <br /> Not every ghost dissolves entirely in the Ocean, the destruction of a Dominion provides a very definite means of playing the odds, and it's a prominent school of thought that the Ferrymen know who needs to go where to destroy a Dominion and actively pursue this end. (And this without getting into the fact that safe passage outright requires a cost in an environment where scarcity is the order of the day.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T18:57:43-07:00","id":1345369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1345159#post1345159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you could change the text, I'm sure you'd put it somewhere that sin eaters are ghosts, since three times over you've<b>(Was Something To Be Here?)</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Read a development post&quot; is not very &quot;literally open in the fluff and mechanics.&quot;-</div> </div> </div> </div>If I wanted to change the text of Geist, I'd become the developer. I don't want to be a developer for any of the gamelines*. I'd rather play in other people's sandboxes.<br /> <br /> That asides, do you not see line break that imply different ideas(or in this case, different approaches that lead to the same conclusion), or is that a deliberate choice?<br /> <br /> Anyways, everyone has got you, so back to main-job-switching.<br /> <br /> *Okay, there's <i>one </i>I want to do that in. It's not Geist. I don't post enough in Geist for it to be Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T23:02:46-07:00","id":1345390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1345197#post1345197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, iirc, it's even said in GtSE that some Rank 1 ghosts completely unaware of their Anchor while they go along with their usual routine. I.e. the Anchor only anchors the ghost's existence to this world, but it has no emotional value for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope! There's a substantial difference between &quot;this thing has no emotional value for the ghost&quot; and &quot;this ghost keeps reliving the events of its death or its unresolved desires, unaware of its situation while still moving within the ranges available to it through its Anchors.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just because the only significance an Anchor might have to a ghost is tangential to the thing itself doesn't mean the ghost doesn't have Feeling Some Way About Something tied up in the mystical qualities that allow that particular thing to bind them to the land of the living.<br /> <br /> There's Rank 1 ghosts that only exist intermittently because they're anchored to <i>dates and times</i>, and them not consciously recognizing that they're dead doesn't change the fact that there's a thing about those parts of the clock and calendar that are core to their identity as ghosts. Generally speaking, if a ghost doesn't recognize they're dead and that's not just because they're new to the experience, it's because they're consumed with acting on the feelings that formed the Anchor to begin with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Bound as ghosts, it's afaik never once outright stated. </div> </div> </div>Chapter Two's section on the Bargain characterizes the geist's offer as something that comes through in the same space where a ghost would start forming Anchors and same chapter's discussion of the Bound's need for connection outright suggests \u2014 alongside &quot;or maybe it's just a psychological reaction to the trauma of death&quot; in a game where it's made abundantly clear that ghosts are people \u2014 that that need is a consequence of being a ghost that happens to have flesh. The Oracle's writeup even says &quot;each and every member of the Bound is dead, meaning they have a perfectly serviceable ghost&quot; and goes on to frame the only obstacle to accessing that ghostly knowledge as needing to incur temporary death again.<br /> <br /> You don't need an outright statement of &quot;the Bound are ghosts&quot; to see a very clear implication that the Bound are only not ghosts in the technical sense of having a living body (and in a game where &quot;one of your limbs or sense organs is a ghost&quot; is a Merit otherwise-normal people can have, the psychological hangups form a rather more significant part of the distinction).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for being metaphysically dead; so are a lot of things in CofD without being ghosts. Vampires being the most obvious example. </div> </div> </div>Most of the other things that are metaphysically dead are undead or animate-unliving beings who are not also conventionally medically alive without directed effort and don't naturally demonstrate powers that are themed after, sourced to, and specifically made to interact with ghosts, who all share a slice of the cosmology with each other because of the way ephemera works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T23:18:01-07:00","id":1345393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1343937-do-not-forget-those-who-will-not-forget-you-ghost-people-are-monsters-who-knew?p=1345390#post1345390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter Two's section on the Bargain characterizes the geist's offer as something that comes through in the same space where a ghost would start forming Anchors and same chapter's discussion of the Bound's need for connection outright suggests \u2014 alongside &quot;or maybe it's just a psychological reaction to the trauma of death&quot; in a game where it's made abundantly clear that ghosts are people \u2014 that that need is a consequence of being a ghost that happens to have flesh. The Oracle's writeup even says &quot;each and every member of the Bound is dead, meaning they have a perfectly serviceable ghost&quot; and goes on to frame the only obstacle to accessing that ghostly knowledge as needing to incur temporary death again.<br /> <br /> You don't need an outright statement of &quot;the Bound are ghosts&quot; to see a very clear implication that the Bound are only not ghosts in the technical sense of having a living body (and in a game where &quot;one of your limbs or sense organs is a ghost&quot; is a Merit otherwise-normal people can have, the psychological hangups form a rather more significant part of the distinction).<br /> <br /> Most of the other things that are metaphysically dead are undead or animate-unliving beings who are not also conventionally medically alive without directed effort and don't naturally demonstrate powers that are themed after, sourced to, and specifically made to interact with ghosts, who all share a slice of the cosmology with each other because of the way ephemera works.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This.<br /> <br /> I may not go as far as William Gibson in assuming readers are geniuses, but I definitely assume they can piece two and two together and don't need hand-holding.<br /> <br /> I do share Gibson's inclination to whiskey when confronted with the limits of that worldview, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-02T00:02:08-07:00","id":1345403,"title":"","content":"This has really made me wonder what it means for a ghost to have an Anchor forced on them through some kind of magic, like an Arisen's Utterances...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}